  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "n-p1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 1200,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "PUBLIC SITE AND JOINING\nEverything a visitor sees before they are a member. Desktop on top, mobile below.\nThe 'wrong address' and 'link expired' screens are part of the set, not edge cases."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 1400,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "MEMBER AREA\nNine screens on desktop, the same nine at 390px below, then the two onboarding states, then the component sheet.\nThe rule running through all of it: the member never maintains their own record."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p3",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "w": 1500,
      "page": "page-3",
      "text": "EXECUTIVE AREA \u2014 THE WHOLE SECTION\nTwelve screens on desktop, ten at 390px below.\nOverview \u00b7 Members \u00b7 Review queue \u00b7 Approve one \u00b7 Events \u00b7 New event \u00b7 One event \u00b7 Attendance \u00b7 Certificates \u00b7 Opportunities \u00b7 Analytics \u00b7 Roles and audit\n\nThis area is designed for someone doing association work at 11pm between deadlines, and for whom the alternative is a WhatsApp group.\nSo every screen leads with what is waiting on them, and the expensive jobs \u2014 approving members, issuing certificates \u2014 are one action for the whole batch."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p3b",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -110,
      "w": 1500,
      "page": "page-3",
      "text": "Attendance is the screen everything else depends on. It works with no network, says so plainly, and keeps a running count \u2014 because if it fails at the hall door, the certificates, the skills and every number in Analytics have nothing to be built from."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p4",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 1000,
      "page": "page-4",
      "text": "NOT YET REWORKED\nThe public event page, still at mobile v1. It belongs to the public site section and gets done properly, both viewports, when that section is revisited."
    }
  ],
